1
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:45,962
‎SPOOKY IN LOVE

2
00:00:47,881 --> 00:00:49,966
‎I should've taken better care of you.

3
00:00:51,259 --> 00:00:52,343
‎It's tough, isn't it?

4
00:00:54,721 --> 00:00:55,805
‎Gang-uk.

5
00:00:58,016 --> 00:00:59,017
‎Should we…

6
00:01:01,352 --> 00:01:02,771
‎break up?

7
00:01:08,193 --> 00:01:09,569
‎Let's call off the engagement.

8
00:01:12,447 --> 00:01:15,283
‎Yeo-ri, did you speak with my grandmother?

9
00:01:18,745 --> 00:01:20,914
‎Don't take what she said to heart.

10
00:01:20,997 --> 00:01:23,249
‎Why believe those things
‎that make no sense?

11
00:01:23,333 --> 00:01:25,085
‎Because I live with something…

12
00:01:27,504 --> 00:01:29,130
‎that makes even less sense.

13
00:01:31,007 --> 00:01:31,925
‎Gang-uk.

14
00:01:33,009 --> 00:01:34,761
‎You had heart surgery?

15
00:01:36,638 --> 00:01:38,056
‎Why didn't you tell me?

16
00:01:39,307 --> 00:01:40,266
‎I'm sorry.

17
00:01:40,975 --> 00:01:42,477
‎I should've told you.

18
00:01:43,228 --> 00:01:46,022
‎I was afraid you'd worry,
‎so I let my chance slip by.

19
00:01:46,105 --> 00:01:47,148
‎Exactly.

20
00:01:48,733 --> 00:01:49,692
‎All that worry…

21
00:01:52,070 --> 00:01:53,196
‎I've had enough of that.

22
00:01:56,741 --> 00:01:58,243
‎For as long as you're with me,

23
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:02,288
‎you'll have to go through things

24
00:02:03,414 --> 00:02:04,916
‎you could do without.

25
00:02:06,334 --> 00:02:07,836
‎And there's no telling

26
00:02:09,504 --> 00:02:10,922
‎when it will even end.

27
00:02:13,216 --> 00:02:14,884
‎Having to stand by and watch

28
00:02:16,010 --> 00:02:18,429
‎and worry with a broken heart…

29
00:02:21,349 --> 00:02:22,684
‎I don't want to do that anymore.

30
00:02:24,435 --> 00:02:26,062
‎-But Yeo-ri…
‎-I…

31
00:02:27,856 --> 00:02:29,858
‎I can barely handle myself.

32
00:02:34,779 --> 00:02:35,613
‎I'm sorry.

33
00:02:37,448 --> 00:02:38,491
‎Let's end it here.

34
00:02:48,001 --> 00:02:49,127
‎Then…

35
00:02:50,128 --> 00:02:52,714
‎do whatever you want
‎when this is all over.

36
00:02:53,590 --> 00:02:54,966
‎You have a target on your back.

37
00:02:55,049 --> 00:02:57,427
‎The prosecutor will give you a rough time.

38
00:02:58,595 --> 00:03:01,556
‎You said you want to protect
‎Reina Group and Siena Hall.

39
00:03:02,557 --> 00:03:04,392
‎We'll do it together, okay?

40
00:03:05,435 --> 00:03:09,063
‎Gang-uk will never leave you,
‎even if his life is at stake.

41
00:03:09,981 --> 00:03:12,525
‎Please, I'm begging you.

42
00:03:15,570 --> 00:03:16,404
‎No.

43
00:03:19,157 --> 00:03:20,450
‎It's best for us both

44
00:03:21,826 --> 00:03:23,161
‎that we end things here.

45
00:03:24,871 --> 00:03:25,872
‎Please understand.

46
00:04:05,912 --> 00:04:07,080
‎Dinner is ready.

47
00:04:07,997 --> 00:04:09,249
‎You must be hungry.

48
00:04:15,338 --> 00:04:16,714
‎Did you really have to do that?

49
00:04:17,715 --> 00:04:19,509
‎What do you mean?

50
00:04:20,134 --> 00:04:21,886
‎You went and talked to Yeo-ri.

51
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:25,974
‎Yes. I met with her.

52
00:04:26,891 --> 00:04:28,059
‎Who cares about zodiac signs?

53
00:04:31,020 --> 00:04:32,939
‎Is that more important
‎than your grandson's feelings?

54
00:04:33,022 --> 00:04:35,566
‎Gang-uk. It's not like that.

55
00:04:35,650 --> 00:04:37,193
‎I asked you, Grandma.

56
00:04:39,445 --> 00:04:40,697
‎To give us a chance.

57
00:04:42,323 --> 00:04:44,534
‎It was the first favor I ever asked.
‎How could you?

58
00:04:45,702 --> 00:04:48,496
‎Do you think I wanted to break you up?

59
00:04:48,579 --> 00:04:50,248
‎It's all for your sake.

60
00:04:50,331 --> 00:04:51,207
‎No.

61
00:04:53,001 --> 00:04:54,085
‎It wasn't for my sake.

62
00:04:55,586 --> 00:04:57,130
‎You did it for your own peace of mind.

63
00:05:04,178 --> 00:05:05,096
‎Gang…

64
00:05:11,060 --> 00:05:12,478
‎Oh, my goodness…

65
00:05:21,821 --> 00:05:24,115
‎I'm sorry. Let's end it here.

66
00:05:47,346 --> 00:05:48,264
‎Hey.

67
00:05:49,766 --> 00:05:52,643
‎There's a lady I volunteer with…

68
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:57,023
‎and she asked if she could meet you

69
00:05:58,191 --> 00:05:59,692
‎over a meal.

70
00:06:00,651 --> 00:06:04,030
‎I owe her greatly,
‎and she's practically a savior of mine.

71
00:06:05,156 --> 00:06:06,157
‎So perhaps…

72
00:06:09,911 --> 00:06:11,412
‎Never mind.

73
00:06:13,706 --> 00:06:15,500
‎We can do it some other time.

74
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:24,342
‎During the prosecution's questioning,

75
00:06:24,425 --> 00:06:27,136
‎try to keep your answers short,
‎preferably just a yes or no.

76
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:30,723
‎If they request additional details,
‎give only the basics at my signal…

77
00:06:33,893 --> 00:06:34,727
‎Ma'am?

78
00:06:40,024 --> 00:06:42,735
‎I'll handle the questions myself.

79
00:06:43,569 --> 00:06:45,530
‎Did you reach
‎the former head of the Art Team

80
00:06:45,613 --> 00:06:46,656
‎who joined Gallery Cheon?

81
00:06:46,739 --> 00:06:48,574
‎We're trying to reach out to her,

82
00:06:49,158 --> 00:06:50,493
‎but it won't be easy.

83
00:06:54,914 --> 00:06:56,082
‎Ma'am.

84
00:06:56,165 --> 00:06:58,543
‎It hasn't been announced yet,
‎but I have intel about our stocks.

85
00:06:59,627 --> 00:07:02,547
‎Someone's buying them before we can.

86
00:07:02,630 --> 00:07:03,464
‎Who is?

87
00:07:03,548 --> 00:07:07,093
‎A branch of DLC Securities
‎is buying up shares in bulk.

88
00:07:07,176 --> 00:07:08,845
‎-DLC Securities?
‎-Yes.

89
00:07:08,928 --> 00:07:12,557
‎After a little digging,
‎I found out that branch is managed

90
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:14,142
‎by none other than CL Group.

91
00:07:20,773 --> 00:07:23,568
‎How is the board reacting to news
‎that I might take over?

92
00:07:23,651 --> 00:07:25,611
‎There hasn't been a notable change.

93
00:07:26,320 --> 00:07:28,448
‎Your succession
‎will be made official soon.

94
00:07:29,115 --> 00:07:30,158
‎Congratulations, sir.

95
00:07:36,164 --> 00:07:38,207
‎You called me for once.
‎What's the occasion?

96
00:07:38,833 --> 00:07:40,209
‎We need to talk.

97
00:07:57,518 --> 00:07:58,895
‎I got this when I was abroad.

98
00:08:01,606 --> 00:08:03,316
‎And I can only spare an hour
‎today at lunch.

99
00:08:14,619 --> 00:08:16,078
‎-Hello, Ms. Song.
‎-Hello, Ms. Song.

100
00:08:16,162 --> 00:08:17,663
‎I'll call Mr. Kang right away.

101
00:08:18,456 --> 00:08:19,916
‎No, leave it.

102
00:08:19,999 --> 00:08:22,502
‎Don't mind me and get back to work.

103
00:08:22,585 --> 00:08:24,795
‎I came by to give Min-hwan a gift.

104
00:08:24,879 --> 00:08:25,922
‎I won't stay long.

105
00:08:30,092 --> 00:08:31,469
‎Someone's been buying Reina shares,

106
00:08:32,094 --> 00:08:33,137
‎and CL Group was behind it.

107
00:08:34,055 --> 00:08:35,973
‎Did you also try to sabotage my deal
‎with Han Se-in?

108
00:08:39,227 --> 00:08:41,979
‎Since when was it?
‎When did you start targeting Reina?

109
00:08:42,063 --> 00:08:43,898
‎Does it matter when it all started?

110
00:08:43,981 --> 00:08:45,900
‎What we do next is what counts.

111
00:08:47,318 --> 00:08:49,737
‎Are you really going to attempt
‎a hostile takeover?

112
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:50,947
‎That's not as easy as it sounds.

113
00:08:55,618 --> 00:08:56,494
‎Kang Min-hwan.

114
00:08:57,203 --> 00:08:58,371
‎Why did you lie to me?

115
00:09:26,566 --> 00:09:27,775
‎You're the one who took it.

116
00:09:28,401 --> 00:09:29,527
‎Ji-hwan's pendant.

117
00:09:46,252 --> 00:09:47,086
‎Who told you that?

118
00:09:47,753 --> 00:09:49,547
‎The paramedic who was
‎at the scene recalled

119
00:09:50,756 --> 00:09:51,841
‎that a family member took it.

120
00:09:55,803 --> 00:09:56,762
‎Fine.

121
00:09:56,846 --> 00:09:58,264
‎Let's say I took it.

122
00:09:58,848 --> 00:10:01,350
‎Why does that matter now?
‎It's just a pendant.

123
00:10:03,769 --> 00:10:04,937
‎At first,

124
00:10:06,647 --> 00:10:08,649
‎I wondered why it had vanished

125
00:10:09,233 --> 00:10:11,819
‎and where it could possibly be now.

126
00:10:11,902 --> 00:10:13,863
‎But now I'm asking different questions.

127
00:10:15,823 --> 00:10:17,783
‎Why are you telling lies?

128
00:10:22,121 --> 00:10:23,122
‎That sounds like

129
00:10:23,748 --> 00:10:25,833
‎you think I'm hiding something.

130
00:10:26,959 --> 00:10:27,835
‎You're going too far.

131
00:10:41,682 --> 00:10:44,226
‎Why didn't you call ahead?
‎I would've stayed behind.

132
00:10:52,985 --> 00:10:56,155
‎Why do you have this?

133
00:10:58,574 --> 00:10:59,492
‎Well…

134
00:10:59,575 --> 00:11:01,369
‎-Did you…
‎-The truth is,

135
00:11:06,082 --> 00:11:07,833
‎I found it after 12 long years.

136
00:11:11,504 --> 00:11:13,589
‎Do you know how much
‎I went through to find that?

137
00:11:14,173 --> 00:11:17,510
‎I barely saved it before
‎the lost-and-found center disposed of it.

138
00:11:18,928 --> 00:11:20,054
‎Did you really?

139
00:11:20,638 --> 00:11:23,057
‎It was the one thing Ji-hwan had with him
‎until his last moment.

140
00:11:23,140 --> 00:11:25,476
‎I wanted to find it
‎and bring it back to you.

141
00:11:27,728 --> 00:11:30,106
‎I meant to gift it to you
‎at his memorial ceremony.

142
00:11:31,982 --> 00:11:32,983
‎Thank you.

143
00:11:36,070 --> 00:11:37,071
‎My dear son.

144
00:11:40,074 --> 00:11:41,367
‎Thank you so much

145
00:11:42,368 --> 00:11:43,411
‎for not forgetting

146
00:11:44,453 --> 00:11:45,788
‎your little brother.

147
00:11:47,456 --> 00:11:48,791
‎How could I forget him?

148
00:11:49,583 --> 00:11:51,710
‎He was my one and only little brother.

149
00:11:53,212 --> 00:11:54,046
‎Right.

150
00:12:06,475 --> 00:12:07,518
‎Mom.

151
00:12:10,646 --> 00:12:12,773
‎So why did you come by today?

152
00:12:12,857 --> 00:12:14,733
‎Why else would I come by?

153
00:12:15,734 --> 00:12:17,153
‎I came to see you, son.

154
00:12:18,237 --> 00:12:21,323
‎I brought you some food
‎and a gift I'd bought.

155
00:12:22,783 --> 00:12:24,160
‎Be sure to eat on time.

156
00:12:26,412 --> 00:12:28,581
‎Oh, I put the gift in your drawer.

157
00:12:30,249 --> 00:12:31,375
‎You're leaving?

158
00:12:31,959 --> 00:12:34,044
‎How about lunch? I have time.

159
00:12:34,545 --> 00:12:36,672
‎Sorry, I have plans today.

160
00:12:37,673 --> 00:12:38,507
‎Maybe next time.

161
00:12:39,592 --> 00:12:40,676
‎I'll see you later.

162
00:12:40,759 --> 00:12:42,261
‎No. I'll see myself out.

163
00:12:44,346 --> 00:12:45,890
‎-Bye then.
‎-Bye.

164
00:12:55,524 --> 00:12:58,152
‎Goodness, you're here early.

165
00:12:58,235 --> 00:12:59,236
‎Good to see you.

166
00:12:59,862 --> 00:13:01,113
‎Please sit.

167
00:13:04,116 --> 00:13:07,411
‎I'm glad Mr. Ma was able to make the time.

168
00:13:07,495 --> 00:13:08,829
‎Well, yes.

169
00:13:10,039 --> 00:13:12,708
‎He hasn't been looking too well lately,

170
00:13:12,791 --> 00:13:15,544
‎and I wanted to treat him to a meal,
‎so this works perfectly.

171
00:13:15,628 --> 00:13:18,255
‎Why is that? Has he been unwell?

172
00:13:19,048 --> 00:13:19,882
‎Well…

173
00:13:21,175 --> 00:13:23,344
‎I didn't know
‎since he didn't tell me at the time,

174
00:13:23,427 --> 00:13:26,555
‎but he was in a bad car accident recently.

175
00:13:26,639 --> 00:13:28,390
‎They even had to run tests on his heart.

176
00:13:28,474 --> 00:13:30,559
‎Gosh, is that true?

177
00:13:30,643 --> 00:13:33,312
‎-Is he okay now?
‎-Yes.

178
00:13:33,395 --> 00:13:35,648
‎He says everything's well and fine,

179
00:13:36,398 --> 00:13:37,983
‎but I can't help but worry.

180
00:13:39,693 --> 00:13:42,196
‎All is well. You needn't worry.

181
00:13:42,279 --> 00:13:44,406
‎Oh, that must be him.

182
00:13:45,199 --> 00:13:46,909
‎Come and say hello.

183
00:13:47,493 --> 00:13:49,495
‎She's the lady I volunteer with.

184
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:53,791
‎I told you
‎she's practically a savior of mine.

185
00:13:55,668 --> 00:13:57,586
‎Hello, I'm Ma Gang-uk.

186
00:13:57,670 --> 00:14:00,172
‎Hello, it's nice to meet you. Please sit.

187
00:14:00,714 --> 00:14:01,549
‎Sit down.

188
00:14:16,981 --> 00:14:20,150
‎You volunteer in a group
‎with my grandmother?

189
00:14:20,234 --> 00:14:24,113
‎Yes. Your grandmother
‎is an admirable lady,

190
00:14:24,196 --> 00:14:25,739
‎and I rely on her a lot.

191
00:14:27,867 --> 00:14:32,162
‎You should join us sometimes
‎instead of just donating money.

192
00:14:32,246 --> 00:14:34,582
‎It'll help you count your blessings later.

193
00:14:38,419 --> 00:14:41,005
‎If it wouldn't be too out of place,

194
00:14:41,088 --> 00:14:44,300
‎I'd like to give you a small gift, Mr. Ma.

195
00:14:45,968 --> 00:14:49,346
‎They say some items
‎are meant for certain people.

196
00:14:49,972 --> 00:14:52,725
‎I happened to come across this
‎right before coming here.

197
00:14:52,808 --> 00:14:56,186
‎Keep it on you,
‎and it's said to protect you from evil

198
00:14:56,270 --> 00:14:57,646
‎and bring good fortune.

199
00:14:57,730 --> 00:15:00,441
‎How considerate of you.

200
00:15:00,524 --> 00:15:01,692
‎Thank you so much.

201
00:15:06,113 --> 00:15:08,490
‎You have a personnel shuffle season
‎coming up soon, right?

202
00:15:09,074 --> 00:15:11,577
‎Make sure you wear this around your neck.

203
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:15,581
‎I bet it'll get you promoted
‎without a problem.

204
00:15:15,664 --> 00:15:18,042
‎Be sure to keep it with you, all right?

205
00:15:27,051 --> 00:15:27,885
‎Ma Gang-uk?

206
00:15:27,968 --> 00:15:30,512
‎-It was good to see you again.
‎-Yes.

207
00:15:31,013 --> 00:15:33,641
‎Why don't you drive her back?

208
00:15:33,724 --> 00:15:36,352
‎No, it's fine. My car will be here soon.

209
00:15:37,186 --> 00:15:39,271
‎Make sure not to skip meals

210
00:15:39,355 --> 00:15:41,732
‎and always take care of your health.

211
00:15:43,150 --> 00:15:44,693
‎I'll do that. Thank you.

212
00:15:44,777 --> 00:15:46,695
‎Please take good care of yourself too.

213
00:15:47,363 --> 00:15:48,197
‎Thanks.

214
00:15:49,573 --> 00:15:51,825
‎-I'll get going then.
‎-Okay, take care.

215
00:15:53,327 --> 00:15:54,703
‎Stay safe.

216
00:15:56,413 --> 00:15:57,414
‎Bye.

217
00:15:58,499 --> 00:15:59,500
‎Goodbye now.

218
00:16:01,543 --> 00:16:04,171
‎-I'll get to it if you're ready.
‎-Okay.

219
00:16:04,254 --> 00:16:06,298
‎-Look straight at the camera.
‎-Okay.

220
00:16:06,382 --> 00:16:07,257
‎-Okay.
‎-Mom?

221
00:16:07,341 --> 00:16:09,593
‎One, two… Ma'am, you look a bit tense.

222
00:16:09,677 --> 00:16:11,470
‎So she ‎wasn't ‎there ‎because ‎of ‎Yeo-ri?

223
00:16:20,312 --> 00:16:21,897
‎PRELIMINARY BACKGROUND REPORT
‎SUBJECT: MA GANG-UK

224
00:16:22,648 --> 00:16:23,857
‎In 2014…

225
00:16:23,941 --> 00:16:25,859
‎2014, HISTORY OF HEART TRANSPLANT

226
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:29,613
‎Don't tell me that Ji-hwan…

227
00:16:40,541 --> 00:16:42,960
‎It looks like we'll need a drink tonight.

228
00:16:43,043 --> 00:16:44,795
‎What? All of a sudden?

229
00:16:45,629 --> 00:16:46,630
‎You saw him.

230
00:16:46,714 --> 00:16:50,092
‎He was sighing all morning,
‎staring at his phone,

231
00:16:50,175 --> 00:16:51,468
‎hoping for a message.

232
00:16:52,136 --> 00:16:53,095
‎They broke up.

233
00:16:53,178 --> 00:16:54,513
‎No way.

234
00:16:54,596 --> 00:16:56,432
‎They went to Singapore together
‎just a while ago.

235
00:16:56,515 --> 00:16:59,852
‎I've known him for years.
‎I can tell at a glance.

236
00:17:00,936 --> 00:17:02,021
‎I'm 100% sure--

237
00:17:03,230 --> 00:17:05,566
‎They 100% broke… Never mind.

238
00:17:29,923 --> 00:17:31,967
‎So what's the pendant
‎you mentioned on the phone?

239
00:17:32,051 --> 00:17:34,386
‎I don't have a photo of it,

240
00:17:34,470 --> 00:17:36,138
‎so I drew what it looked like.

241
00:17:41,894 --> 00:17:44,855
‎CONTACTS

242
00:17:49,651 --> 00:17:51,236
‎Mr. Ma.

243
00:17:51,737 --> 00:17:53,072
‎How about dinner today?

244
00:17:53,155 --> 00:17:56,450
‎Our Hyeong-min here…

245
00:17:56,533 --> 00:17:59,078
‎You said you found a great diner, right?

246
00:17:59,161 --> 00:18:02,122
‎Yes, that place?
‎The food there is amazing.

247
00:18:02,206 --> 00:18:03,749
‎-You two can go.
‎-Just us?

248
00:18:03,832 --> 00:18:05,167
‎No, we're a team.

249
00:18:05,250 --> 00:18:08,295
‎Yeah, Mr. Ma.
‎There's a great diner nearby.

250
00:18:08,378 --> 00:18:10,297
‎-It's just what you'd like.
‎-Totally.

251
00:18:10,380 --> 00:18:12,091
‎I have lots to do today.

252
00:18:12,174 --> 00:18:15,135
‎Okay then. I'll be brutally honest.

253
00:18:15,928 --> 00:18:17,304
‎It's Hyeong-min.

254
00:18:17,387 --> 00:18:19,848
‎Can I tell him? Whatever, I'll say it.

255
00:18:19,932 --> 00:18:23,143
‎Poor Hyeong-min has a serious dilemma.

256
00:18:28,107 --> 00:18:30,150
‎Mr. Ma. The thing is…

257
00:18:30,234 --> 00:18:33,153
‎Hey, it can wait.
‎Talk about it over dinner.

258
00:18:33,237 --> 00:18:34,613
‎You two go ahead then.

259
00:18:34,696 --> 00:18:36,532
‎-I'll join you when I'm done.
‎-Okay.

260
00:18:43,497 --> 00:18:45,749
‎That's enough. You can stop now.

261
00:18:46,333 --> 00:18:48,001
‎-You've suffered enough.
‎-Sorry.

262
00:18:48,085 --> 00:18:49,461
‎I'm really sorry.

263
00:18:50,546 --> 00:18:52,005
‎Yes, Grandma.

264
00:18:52,089 --> 00:18:55,717
‎We can buy up more than CL did
‎with our existing funds.

265
00:18:56,301 --> 00:18:57,594
‎You don't have to worry.

266
00:18:58,428 --> 00:18:59,263
‎Okay.

267
00:19:04,017 --> 00:19:06,687
‎Ma'am, you're expected
‎at the prosecutors' office tomorrow.

268
00:19:06,770 --> 00:19:08,230
‎GANG-UK

269
00:19:20,576 --> 00:19:22,119
‎Your food is here.

270
00:19:22,744 --> 00:19:25,372
‎-Thank you.
‎-Finally, our food's here.

271
00:19:33,380 --> 00:19:35,799
‎-Let's eat.
‎-Okay. Mr. Ma.

272
00:19:35,883 --> 00:19:37,134
‎Come and try this.

273
00:19:40,262 --> 00:19:42,764
‎I had this not long ago,

274
00:19:42,848 --> 00:19:44,558
‎and I thought of you right away.

275
00:19:44,641 --> 00:19:46,685
‎You love spicy food, don't you?

276
00:19:46,768 --> 00:19:49,563
‎Take a bite and let go of all the stress.

277
00:19:50,522 --> 00:19:52,065
‎-You should eat too.
‎-Try it.

278
00:19:54,151 --> 00:19:56,153
‎Look at this. Look at the meat.

279
00:19:56,236 --> 00:19:58,322
‎Just look at how thick and meaty it is.

280
00:19:58,405 --> 00:20:01,408
‎Watch it be nice and chewy too.
‎I won't be able to take it.

281
00:20:01,992 --> 00:20:03,869
‎No way. This is…

282
00:20:03,952 --> 00:20:06,997
‎This is too much to handle.
‎How can it be juicy too?

283
00:20:07,080 --> 00:20:09,666
‎Mr. Ma, have a taste.

284
00:20:09,750 --> 00:20:10,792
‎Open up.

285
00:20:15,547 --> 00:20:17,674
‎-Isn't it good?
‎-Yeah, it's nice and spicy.

286
00:20:17,758 --> 00:20:18,800
‎Right?

287
00:20:18,884 --> 00:20:22,721
‎Have some good food
‎and don't overthink things.

288
00:20:22,804 --> 00:20:24,640
‎So what's your dilemma, Hyeong-min?

289
00:20:25,766 --> 00:20:27,684
‎Oh, my dilemma?

290
00:20:27,768 --> 00:20:28,894
‎It kind of solved itself.

291
00:20:28,977 --> 00:20:31,772
‎The dilemma is yours, Mr. Ma.

292
00:20:31,855 --> 00:20:33,065
‎What's going on with Ms. Cheon?

293
00:20:33,148 --> 00:20:35,525
‎You've been staring
‎at that necklace all day.

294
00:20:35,609 --> 00:20:36,944
‎Something's going on
‎between you and Ms. Cheon.

295
00:20:38,403 --> 00:20:39,238
‎She wants to break up.

296
00:20:41,490 --> 00:20:42,616
‎And she won't take my calls.

297
00:20:44,201 --> 00:20:45,160
‎No way.

298
00:20:45,744 --> 00:20:47,537
‎Seeing how things are tough right now,

299
00:20:47,621 --> 00:20:50,791
‎she's probably looking out for you
‎by keeping a distance.

300
00:20:50,874 --> 00:20:54,253
‎She'll definitely call you back
‎the moment things blow over.

301
00:20:54,336 --> 00:20:55,379
‎Don't you worry.

302
00:20:57,506 --> 00:21:00,175
‎By the way, this looks quite mystical.

303
00:21:00,259 --> 00:21:02,010
‎Is it a gift for Ms. Cheon?

304
00:21:02,094 --> 00:21:03,345
‎No.

305
00:21:03,428 --> 00:21:05,222
‎It's something she was looking for,

306
00:21:05,889 --> 00:21:07,349
‎and it happened to end up with me.

307
00:21:08,642 --> 00:21:12,187
‎Did it find its way to me
‎to bring me back to her?

308
00:21:12,271 --> 00:21:14,398
‎Really? Wow.

309
00:21:14,481 --> 00:21:17,192
‎You two must really be meant to be.

310
00:21:19,403 --> 00:21:20,320
‎What's this?

311
00:21:20,404 --> 00:21:22,114
‎The mark of the person who made it.

312
00:21:22,197 --> 00:21:23,907
‎It's a seal of a sort.

313
00:21:24,658 --> 00:21:26,535
‎It doesn't look like it. How do you know?

314
00:21:26,618 --> 00:21:27,744
‎Come on.

315
00:21:28,287 --> 00:21:31,832
‎I've been in this line of work
‎for years, man.

316
00:21:31,915 --> 00:21:34,584
‎I've seen thousands of necklaces
‎like this as evidence…

317
00:21:34,668 --> 00:21:37,170
‎Give it back. You'll curse it.

318
00:21:37,254 --> 00:21:38,505
‎"Curse it"? What…

319
00:21:39,965 --> 00:21:40,841
‎Dig in.

320
00:21:42,467 --> 00:21:44,678
‎Seriously, this is so…

321
00:21:46,555 --> 00:21:48,348
‎This is so good, Hyeong-min.

322
00:21:48,432 --> 00:21:51,143
‎-Try the side menu too. It's to die for.
‎-Yeah?

323
00:21:52,102 --> 00:21:53,437
‎Let me put some on your plate.

324
00:21:54,855 --> 00:21:57,899
‎-This thing? It's good?
‎-Yes.

325
00:22:24,176 --> 00:22:25,469
‎Man, my back.

326
00:22:32,225 --> 00:22:34,102
‎It's so uncomfortable.

327
00:22:35,187 --> 00:22:36,938
‎How did she manage for so long?

328
00:22:42,986 --> 00:22:44,821
‎Yeo-ri…

329
00:22:57,459 --> 00:23:00,295
‎You said you want to protect
‎Reina Group and Siena Hall.

330
00:23:00,879 --> 00:23:02,714
‎We'll do it together, okay?

331
00:23:02,798 --> 00:23:03,924
‎Good luck to us.

332
00:23:04,007 --> 00:23:05,300
‎-When she's struggling,
‎-You got this!

333
00:23:06,176 --> 00:23:07,969
‎I'll never let her go through it alone.

334
00:23:09,221 --> 00:23:11,890
‎No matter where she is or where I am,

335
00:23:13,558 --> 00:23:15,060
‎I'll be there by her side.

336
00:23:25,237 --> 00:23:26,905
‎-That's her.
‎-She's coming.

337
00:23:26,988 --> 00:23:28,990
‎-Don't get too close.
‎-Step back.

338
00:23:29,074 --> 00:23:31,076
‎-Step back.
‎-That's her.

339
00:23:31,785 --> 00:23:32,786
‎When they ask questions,

340
00:23:32,869 --> 00:23:35,163
‎just tell them you'll cooperate
‎with the investigation.

341
00:23:45,173 --> 00:23:46,299
‎Careful, coming through.

342
00:23:46,383 --> 00:23:49,386
‎Ms. Cheon, how do you feel
‎about today's questioning?

343
00:23:49,469 --> 00:23:52,389
‎Which allegations
‎will you be clarifying today?

344
00:23:52,472 --> 00:23:55,433
‎Many are disappointed
‎by the current allegations.

345
00:23:55,517 --> 00:23:56,768
‎Do you have any comments?

346
00:23:56,852 --> 00:23:58,979
‎Ms. Cheon, did you really embezzle funds?

347
00:23:59,062 --> 00:24:02,023
‎Your stocks are plummeting.
‎Do you have any plans to step down?

348
00:24:05,944 --> 00:24:08,029
‎SEOUL DISTRICT PROSECUTORS' OFFICE

349
00:24:08,947 --> 00:24:09,990
‎Please stand back.

350
00:24:10,073 --> 00:24:13,577
‎It would be best
‎if you stay put right now.

351
00:24:13,660 --> 00:24:15,036
‎He's right, Mr. Ma.

352
00:24:15,120 --> 00:24:17,497
‎Thankfully, Prosecutor Im is in charge.

353
00:24:17,581 --> 00:24:19,040
‎She's just as fair

354
00:24:19,541 --> 00:24:21,877
‎and by the book as you are,
‎so please…

355
00:24:21,960 --> 00:24:22,878
‎Mr. Ma.

356
00:24:25,839 --> 00:24:28,884
‎First, regarding
‎the embezzlement and negligence.

357
00:24:29,843 --> 00:24:31,219
‎I did no such thing.

358
00:24:31,803 --> 00:24:34,097
‎From now on,
‎anyone who publishes false reports

359
00:24:34,181 --> 00:24:36,516
‎will be held accountable to the end.

360
00:24:37,100 --> 00:24:40,187
‎And regarding my position as CEO,

361
00:24:41,229 --> 00:24:44,065
‎we're facing a crisis
‎that happened within the hotel.

362
00:24:44,149 --> 00:24:46,193
‎As CEO, I will take responsibility

363
00:24:46,276 --> 00:24:47,986
‎and put everything back on track.

364
00:24:48,653 --> 00:24:50,780
‎However, for any false accusations,

365
00:24:52,157 --> 00:24:54,451
‎I will take decisive legal action.

366
00:24:55,076 --> 00:24:56,870
‎Did that answer your questions?

367
00:24:57,662 --> 00:25:01,958
‎What will you do about the lost profits
‎and damages the shareholders will face?

368
00:25:02,042 --> 00:25:05,879
‎-Any comments about the investigation?
‎-Ms. Cheon! Ms. Cheon!

369
00:25:06,463 --> 00:25:07,547
‎Hey, Im.

370
00:25:07,631 --> 00:25:09,549
‎I won't say much. Just do it by the book.

371
00:25:09,633 --> 00:25:12,052
‎Must you say the obvious?

372
00:25:15,805 --> 00:25:17,182
‎Thank you for coming.

373
00:25:17,265 --> 00:25:19,309
‎I'm sorry we meet again
‎under such circumstances.

374
00:25:20,018 --> 00:25:21,019
‎Would you like some tea first?

375
00:25:21,102 --> 00:25:23,063
‎No. Let's get straight to it.

376
00:25:23,146 --> 00:25:24,314
‎Come this way, please.

377
00:25:35,450 --> 00:25:38,411
‎You made improper solicitations between
‎Yeeon and Assemblyman Park Jin-dong…

378
00:25:38,495 --> 00:25:39,496
‎Before we get into that,

379
00:25:40,580 --> 00:25:42,540
‎I'd like to clarify something first.

380
00:25:44,042 --> 00:25:48,380
‎I have never met or had contact
‎with Park in a private setting,

381
00:25:48,463 --> 00:25:50,715
‎let alone a public one.

382
00:25:51,424 --> 00:25:53,301
‎I was abroad on a business trip
‎when he met my family

383
00:25:53,385 --> 00:25:54,594
‎to discuss my cousin's engagement.

384
00:25:55,679 --> 00:25:59,057
‎If needed, I'm willing to let you
‎access my phone records.

385
00:25:59,683 --> 00:26:00,684
‎To be honest,

386
00:26:01,977 --> 00:26:05,230
‎don't you think Director Ok Gye-hui
‎is a more likely connection

387
00:26:05,730 --> 00:26:07,232
‎when it comes to Assemblyman Park?

388
00:26:08,108 --> 00:26:10,485
‎I wonder if they had to
‎rely heavily on the media

389
00:26:11,027 --> 00:26:12,988
‎to forcibly connect me
‎to a story about--

390
00:26:13,071 --> 00:26:14,948
‎That's for us to prove.

391
00:26:15,031 --> 00:26:16,283
‎There's one more thing.

392
00:26:18,410 --> 00:26:19,869
‎We have a flash drive with evidence

393
00:26:19,953 --> 00:26:23,873
‎suggesting Gallery Cheon's Director Ok
‎and Kim So-hui, Reina's ex-Art Team head,

394
00:26:23,957 --> 00:26:27,460
‎colluded to embezzle from the company
‎by dereliction of duty.

395
00:26:27,544 --> 00:26:30,046
‎It contains a list of paintings
‎purchased by Reina Hotel

396
00:26:30,130 --> 00:26:32,799
‎and the difference between
‎the market price and actual trading price.

397
00:26:33,425 --> 00:26:35,468
‎I'd like to formally request
‎an investigation.

398
00:26:36,761 --> 00:26:38,638
‎I just ask that you be fair

399
00:26:39,514 --> 00:26:40,765
‎and by the book.

400
00:26:57,991 --> 00:27:01,119
‎REPORT MISCONDUCT
‎OF CORRUPT PUBLIC OFFICIAL

401
00:27:15,467 --> 00:27:18,094
‎-Ms. Cheon, did you say much?
‎-Did you cooperate fully?

402
00:27:18,178 --> 00:27:20,221
‎What did your lawyer say?

403
00:27:20,305 --> 00:27:22,182
‎-Comments, please.
‎-How do you feel now?

404
00:27:22,265 --> 00:27:23,725
‎Coming through!

405
00:27:23,808 --> 00:27:25,643
‎-Make way.
‎-You can't stay here.

406
00:27:25,727 --> 00:27:28,646
‎Ms. Cheon, can you share
‎how you feel after today's questioning?

407
00:27:28,730 --> 00:27:31,483
‎Do you still insist
‎you had no political involvement?

408
00:27:33,193 --> 00:27:36,613
‎Do you deny some of the embezzled funds
‎went to lobbying politicians?

409
00:27:36,696 --> 00:27:38,698
‎Were you notified of further questioning?

410
00:27:38,782 --> 00:27:41,201
‎-Anything to say?
‎-Ms. Cheon!

411
00:28:44,139 --> 00:28:45,056
‎Stop…

412
00:28:46,057 --> 00:28:47,058
‎the car.

413
00:28:51,646 --> 00:28:52,564
‎Gang-uk.

414
00:28:53,064 --> 00:28:54,441
‎Spare me some time.

415
00:28:55,859 --> 00:28:56,860
‎It won't take long.

416
00:29:04,826 --> 00:29:05,869
‎What is it you want to say?

417
00:29:10,915 --> 00:29:11,750
‎What's that?

418
00:29:17,839 --> 00:29:19,507
‎-This is…
‎-So it is the one.

419
00:29:20,550 --> 00:29:21,843
‎Where did you get this?

420
00:29:21,926 --> 00:29:25,346
‎Someone from my grandmother's
‎volunteer group gave it to me.

421
00:29:25,430 --> 00:29:27,432
‎She told me that the necklace

422
00:29:27,515 --> 00:29:29,726
‎wards off bad energy.

423
00:29:29,809 --> 00:29:32,145
‎I thought the shape looked similar.

424
00:29:33,480 --> 00:29:34,773
‎Gang-uk, could I…

425
00:29:35,356 --> 00:29:37,317
‎keep this for the time being?

426
00:29:37,400 --> 00:29:38,318
‎Of course.

427
00:29:39,194 --> 00:29:42,614
‎If you look on the back,
‎there's a pattern on it.

428
00:29:43,239 --> 00:29:45,408
‎Apparently, it's a kind of seal
‎by the maker.

429
00:29:46,284 --> 00:29:49,746
‎I can look into where it was made
‎if you need me to.

430
00:29:51,956 --> 00:29:53,958
‎Yes. Can you do that for me?

431
00:29:56,961 --> 00:29:58,755
‎Can you do something for me too?

432
00:30:00,715 --> 00:30:03,510
‎You stay right where you are.
‎I'll come to you.

433
00:30:06,387 --> 00:30:10,558
‎That way, you won't be breaking
‎your promise to my grandma.

434
00:30:49,055 --> 00:30:51,140
‎The report on the defendant tells me

435
00:30:51,224 --> 00:30:53,101
‎they're going to deny everything.

436
00:30:53,184 --> 00:30:56,437
‎I already put sticky notes
‎on all the parts

437
00:30:56,521 --> 00:30:58,523
‎where the evidence
‎differs from his statement.

438
00:30:58,606 --> 00:31:00,650
‎If they deny anything,

439
00:31:00,733 --> 00:31:02,694
‎-just show them that.
‎-Okay.

440
00:31:02,777 --> 00:31:04,654
‎You keep all the nice stuff to yourself,

441
00:31:05,655 --> 00:31:07,073
‎don't you?

442
00:31:07,866 --> 00:31:10,451
‎Also, I heard the defense attorney

443
00:31:10,535 --> 00:31:13,913
‎can be a bit difficult to deal with.

444
00:31:13,997 --> 00:31:16,666
‎You need to put them in their place
‎from the start.

445
00:31:16,749 --> 00:31:19,544
‎Have this before you go.
‎It'll recharge your energy.

446
00:31:19,627 --> 00:31:21,629
‎Fuel up and do your thing.

447
00:31:23,715 --> 00:31:24,591
‎I do feel fueled up.

448
00:31:27,343 --> 00:31:28,428
‎Hey.

449
00:31:29,429 --> 00:31:31,139
‎-Is it true?
‎-What is?

450
00:31:31,222 --> 00:31:34,559
‎You blew the whistle on Ok Gye-dong
‎to the Ministry of Justice?

451
00:31:34,642 --> 00:31:35,476
‎Yes.

452
00:31:38,813 --> 00:31:40,106
‎What were you thinking?

453
00:31:40,690 --> 00:31:42,734
‎You could become sidelined.

454
00:31:42,817 --> 00:31:44,360
‎Just go on the training program.

455
00:31:45,111 --> 00:31:47,363
‎It's called sharing information,
‎not blowing the whistle.

456
00:31:48,615 --> 00:31:51,451
‎I have a trial to attend,
‎so if you'll excuse me.

457
00:31:52,243 --> 00:31:54,162
‎Hyeong-min. Give him one.

458
00:31:54,245 --> 00:31:55,163
‎Okay.

459
00:31:56,456 --> 00:31:58,958
‎Yes. I'll take care of it,
‎Mr. Senior Secretary.

460
00:32:00,752 --> 00:32:02,211
‎I'm sorry for causing you concern

461
00:32:02,295 --> 00:32:03,922
‎during such sensitive times.

462
00:32:05,423 --> 00:32:06,257
‎Yes, sir.

463
00:32:09,886 --> 00:32:11,679
‎Did that bastard
‎Ma Gang-uk blow the whistle?

464
00:32:11,763 --> 00:32:12,972
‎I apologize, sir.

465
00:32:13,556 --> 00:32:15,350
‎But he's a good kid…

466
00:32:15,433 --> 00:32:16,434
‎The election's coming up!

467
00:32:25,944 --> 00:32:26,903
‎It's me.

468
00:32:27,403 --> 00:32:30,281
‎Make sure Chief Prosecutor Ok Gye-dong
‎undergoes a thorough investigation.

469
00:32:30,949 --> 00:32:34,369
‎As for Park Jin-dong,
‎besides the illegal lobbying and bribery,

470
00:32:36,204 --> 00:32:38,957
‎he has shares in borrowed accounts,
‎so get the warrant to cover that too.

471
00:32:39,624 --> 00:32:40,875
‎And get a motion for consent to arrest.

472
00:32:45,338 --> 00:32:46,381
‎Get out!

473
00:33:02,355 --> 00:33:04,524
‎Given all the evidence,
‎I don't think there will be a way out.

474
00:33:05,108 --> 00:33:06,818
‎Ms. Kim, Reina's Head of Art Team…

475
00:33:06,901 --> 00:33:10,780
‎Right. You're Gallery Cheon's
‎associate director now, aren't you?

476
00:33:11,864 --> 00:33:13,741
‎You did know that

477
00:33:13,825 --> 00:33:16,869
‎Director Ok Gye-hui's brother
‎is a chief prosecutor here, right?

478
00:33:18,037 --> 00:33:19,497
‎This doesn't look good.

479
00:33:19,580 --> 00:33:21,749
‎You might end up
‎taking the fall for it all.

480
00:33:30,466 --> 00:33:31,300
‎I'll…

481
00:33:31,884 --> 00:33:33,845
‎tell you everything.

482
00:33:38,307 --> 00:33:41,269
‎Do you consent to
‎your interview being recorded?

483
00:33:49,819 --> 00:33:53,281
‎VIDEO RECORDING CONSENT FORM, KIM SO-HUI

484
00:33:53,364 --> 00:33:55,116
‎Assemblyman Park Jin-dong,
‎who was facing arrest,

485
00:33:55,199 --> 00:33:58,327
‎was found dead in his district office.

486
00:33:58,411 --> 00:34:00,329
‎He was tied to bribery
‎involving Yeeon Museum of Art,

487
00:34:00,413 --> 00:34:01,789
‎trading stocks in borrowed names,

488
00:34:01,873 --> 00:34:06,127
‎and pressuring officials to
‎reroute ‎a highway that was to pass by--

489
00:34:10,089 --> 00:34:11,090
‎Oh, no.

490
00:34:12,967 --> 00:34:13,926
‎Mom.

491
00:34:15,970 --> 00:34:19,015
‎-What's wrong?
‎-Assemblyman Park Jin-dong…

492
00:34:20,016 --> 00:34:20,975
‎killed himself.

493
00:34:24,687 --> 00:34:25,772
‎Hold on.

494
00:34:25,855 --> 00:34:28,858
‎We must remain calm at a time like this.

495
00:34:36,282 --> 00:34:37,575
‎Hey, Gye-dong.

496
00:34:38,367 --> 00:34:41,496
‎With what's happened to Park Jin-dong,

497
00:34:42,121 --> 00:34:43,664
‎what will happen to us?

498
00:34:43,748 --> 00:34:45,333
‎What do you mean?

499
00:34:45,416 --> 00:34:48,252
‎You can't indict a dead man.
‎His case is closed.

500
00:34:49,587 --> 00:34:50,671
‎By the way, Gye-hui.

501
00:34:50,755 --> 00:34:53,800
‎-Can't we play that card now?
‎-Which card?

502
00:34:56,010 --> 00:34:58,846
‎You mean the district
‎chief prosecutor's wife?

503
00:35:00,264 --> 00:35:02,308
‎Okay. Hang up so I can think.

504
00:35:08,940 --> 00:35:09,774
‎But then again,

505
00:35:09,857 --> 00:35:11,776
‎I spent a fortune
‎on paintings to bribe her.

506
00:35:12,693 --> 00:35:15,988
‎She was an insurance policy
‎we took out for a time like this.

507
00:35:17,281 --> 00:35:19,742
‎It's all about getting the timing right.

508
00:35:22,036 --> 00:35:25,248
‎Man, how can they be so predictable?

509
00:35:25,331 --> 00:35:28,459
‎Do they think transfers are a joke?
‎Now they want me at a regional branch?

510
00:35:29,210 --> 00:35:31,754
‎The district chief wanted you
‎sent to a remote island,

511
00:35:31,838 --> 00:35:33,464
‎but I had you assigned there instead.

512
00:35:33,548 --> 00:35:35,383
‎-Come on, Sang-ho!
‎-You punk.

513
00:35:35,925 --> 00:35:38,970
‎The Ministry of Justice
‎just launched an internal inspection,

514
00:35:39,053 --> 00:35:40,513
‎thanks to your whistleblowing.

515
00:35:40,596 --> 00:35:43,474
‎-I did what I had to.
‎-Exactly.

516
00:35:43,558 --> 00:35:45,434
‎Take responsibility for what you did.

517
00:35:46,894 --> 00:35:49,438
‎There's still some time,
‎so hand over your cases thoroughly.

518
00:35:53,484 --> 00:35:55,736
‎I should just quit being a prosecutor.

519
00:35:56,320 --> 00:35:57,405
‎Please don't quit.

520
00:35:59,448 --> 00:36:00,783
‎Life is so…

521
00:36:01,784 --> 00:36:02,618
‎unfair.

522
00:36:04,912 --> 00:36:06,289
‎This is nothing new.

523
00:36:06,372 --> 00:36:08,833
‎I'll hand over my cases before I leave.
‎You can go home.

524
00:36:08,916 --> 00:36:10,918
‎-Mr. Ma.
‎-Yeah?

525
00:36:11,002 --> 00:36:12,670
‎-The thing you asked me to look into.
‎-Yeah.

526
00:36:12,753 --> 00:36:16,632
‎I did some digging about
‎where that necklace was made.

527
00:36:17,675 --> 00:36:18,509
‎I found it.

528
00:36:19,552 --> 00:36:20,469
‎How?

529
00:36:20,553 --> 00:36:23,181
‎-There was nothing on social media.
‎-Okay.

530
00:36:23,264 --> 00:36:26,976
‎I had to search
‎secret forums on the dark web,

531
00:36:27,059 --> 00:36:29,979
‎and I found someone
‎who posted the pendant to brag about it.

532
00:36:30,062 --> 00:36:31,689
‎The person who posted about it

533
00:36:31,772 --> 00:36:34,650
‎is someone from a family
‎everyone knows by name.

534
00:36:34,734 --> 00:36:37,361
‎Oh, and the pattern
‎on the back of the pendant

535
00:36:37,445 --> 00:36:40,740
‎serves as a pass that allows you
‎to meet the person who made it.

536
00:36:41,782 --> 00:36:43,409
‎-I'll send you the link.
‎-Okay.

537
00:36:43,492 --> 00:36:45,244
‎How are you so good at finding stuff?

538
00:36:45,328 --> 00:36:46,537
‎Hyeong-min, you…

539
00:36:46,621 --> 00:36:47,914
‎What are you really like?

540
00:36:47,997 --> 00:36:50,499
‎What kind of life did you lead
‎to be so good at this?

541
00:36:52,001 --> 00:36:53,169
‎When I was in the military,

542
00:36:53,961 --> 00:36:56,505
‎there was this really nasty guy
‎a rank or two above me.

543
00:36:56,589 --> 00:36:58,841
‎I did everything to track him down after…

544
00:36:58,925 --> 00:37:00,259
‎GANG-UK

545
00:37:00,343 --> 00:37:02,178
‎I have something to tell you
‎about the pendant.

546
00:37:02,261 --> 00:37:03,387
‎Please pick up.

547
00:37:04,931 --> 00:37:06,557
‎GANG-UK

548
00:37:09,644 --> 00:37:10,519
‎Hello?

549
00:37:11,270 --> 00:37:13,481
‎What about the pendant?

550
00:37:13,564 --> 00:37:15,358
‎I found out where it was made.

551
00:37:16,400 --> 00:37:17,860
‎-Really?
‎-Yes.

552
00:37:17,944 --> 00:37:20,363
‎Where is it? Can you tell me?

553
00:37:20,446 --> 00:37:21,822
‎No.

554
00:37:23,074 --> 00:37:24,659
‎I'll tell you if we go together.

555
00:37:32,917 --> 00:37:35,461
‎It's a place
‎that caters to the high class.

556
00:37:35,544 --> 00:37:36,754
‎I called ahead.

557
00:37:51,435 --> 00:37:54,146
‎Are you the one who made this?

558
00:37:54,230 --> 00:37:55,523
‎Not me.

559
00:37:56,107 --> 00:37:59,026
‎This is my mother's work.
‎She died two years ago.

560
00:38:10,121 --> 00:38:12,081
‎It looks great on you. You can keep it.

561
00:38:42,069 --> 00:38:43,404
‎This item

562
00:38:43,988 --> 00:38:45,406
‎changed your fate.

563
00:38:46,615 --> 00:38:49,201
‎This pendant belongs to someone else,
‎doesn't it?

564
00:38:51,454 --> 00:38:52,872
‎Yes, that's right.

565
00:38:52,955 --> 00:38:55,082
‎You should've let go,
‎however bad you felt.

566
00:38:55,916 --> 00:38:58,336
‎You brought back a spirit
‎that was meant for the afterlife.

567
00:38:59,503 --> 00:39:01,255
‎-Pardon?
‎-You brought back

568
00:39:01,339 --> 00:39:03,007
‎the owner of this pendant.

569
00:39:04,342 --> 00:39:07,553
‎The dead should remain with the dead,
‎and the living should go on living.

570
00:39:07,636 --> 00:39:09,138
‎There are two different paths.

571
00:39:09,764 --> 00:39:11,265
‎Yet you, a mere human,

572
00:39:11,766 --> 00:39:13,768
‎changed the divine order of things.

573
00:39:15,144 --> 00:39:17,146
‎Consider it the price you have to pay.

574
00:39:34,288 --> 00:39:35,331
‎Your hand is cold.

575
00:39:37,541 --> 00:39:38,918
‎You see things you shouldn't, right?

576
00:39:40,795 --> 00:39:44,882
‎Most people give off heat,
‎which keeps ghosts at bay.

577
00:39:44,965 --> 00:39:47,593
‎Cold beings cannot approach
‎those who carry warmth.

578
00:39:48,427 --> 00:39:49,553
‎That is the order of things.

579
00:39:51,263 --> 00:39:54,683
‎You've hardly ever held the hand
‎of a living person, have you?

580
00:39:57,686 --> 00:39:58,854
‎Well, yes.

581
00:39:59,438 --> 00:40:01,774
‎Other than for brief moments…

582
00:40:01,857 --> 00:40:05,069
‎It's only through human touch
‎that we're filled with warmth.

583
00:40:07,113 --> 00:40:10,449
‎You would've never known
‎how cold your hands were.

584
00:40:15,371 --> 00:40:18,040
‎Is there any way
‎to stop her from seeing ghosts?

585
00:40:20,042 --> 00:40:21,752
‎She's paying for disrupting
‎nature's order.

586
00:40:23,295 --> 00:40:25,297
‎The only way out is to pay with a life.

587
00:40:41,313 --> 00:40:43,107
‎Don't worry too much about what she said.

588
00:40:44,400 --> 00:40:46,235
‎Let's find another way together.

589
00:40:48,904 --> 00:40:49,738
‎Are you all right?

590
00:40:53,826 --> 00:40:56,912
‎If our lives changed track
‎because of this pendant,

591
00:40:57,997 --> 00:40:59,165
‎then that means

592
00:41:00,291 --> 00:41:02,376
‎Ji-hwan really died because of me.

593
00:41:04,753 --> 00:41:06,255
‎I remember he said to me…

594
00:41:06,922 --> 00:41:08,799
‎I don't mind it
‎if it means I can save you.

595
00:41:09,758 --> 00:41:11,302
‎If something does happen,

596
00:41:12,011 --> 00:41:14,430
‎you have to live. I'll die instead.

597
00:41:17,308 --> 00:41:19,602
‎I see it a little differently.

598
00:41:21,353 --> 00:41:23,397
‎There's no way to prove

599
00:41:23,481 --> 00:41:28,360
‎whether it was because of the pendant
‎or simply the fate you two shared.

600
00:41:30,196 --> 00:41:32,323
‎Even if it was because of the pendant,

601
00:41:33,324 --> 00:41:35,117
‎considering what Ji-hwan said,

602
00:41:35,826 --> 00:41:39,288
‎he probably thought of it
‎as a gift and not a sacrifice.

603
00:41:40,164 --> 00:41:41,916
‎So don't blame yourself too much.

604
00:41:51,592 --> 00:41:53,219
‎Since it was given to you,

605
00:41:54,512 --> 00:41:56,013
‎you should hold onto it.

606
00:42:16,951 --> 00:42:18,244
‎Park Seung-jae.

607
00:42:18,327 --> 00:42:22,748
‎You're released for no more than five days
‎to attend your father's funeral.

608
00:42:22,831 --> 00:42:24,083
‎Send him off in peace.

609
00:42:24,750 --> 00:42:25,584
‎And take our calls.

610
00:42:46,021 --> 00:42:47,064
‎What the hell is this?

611
00:42:49,108 --> 00:42:51,527
‎There isn't a single soul in sight.

612
00:42:56,240 --> 00:42:57,241
‎Yes, Chief.

613
00:42:59,410 --> 00:43:00,244
‎What?

614
00:43:00,327 --> 00:43:02,162
‎Take back the warrant request?

615
00:43:04,123 --> 00:43:05,291
‎That's nonsense, Chief--

616
00:43:10,462 --> 00:43:11,880
‎Yes, ma'am.

617
00:43:12,464 --> 00:43:15,342
‎I won't forget how you helped us.

618
00:43:15,843 --> 00:43:17,469
‎Yes, of course.

619
00:43:17,553 --> 00:43:19,805
‎He must become
‎the next prosecutor general.

620
00:43:19,888 --> 00:43:23,392
‎I'll make sure I'm never
‎a hindrance to his career…

621
00:43:37,031 --> 00:43:39,408
‎I've talked things over with the board.

622
00:43:39,908 --> 00:43:42,953
‎We'll announce it
‎at Ji-hwan's memorial ceremony.

623
00:43:44,330 --> 00:43:45,164
‎Mother…

624
00:43:54,757 --> 00:43:58,427
‎We've confirmed Ms. Song has not contacted
‎Prosecutor Ma since then.

625
00:43:59,428 --> 00:44:00,304
‎Is that so?

626
00:44:00,387 --> 00:44:03,724
‎And the Office of Strategy and Planning
‎has started the succession protocol.

627
00:44:14,735 --> 00:44:16,153
‎Defendant Park Seung-jae.

628
00:44:16,236 --> 00:44:18,947
‎You have absconded
‎from your allocated residence,

629
00:44:19,031 --> 00:44:21,116
‎breaking the conditions
‎of your temporary release.

630
00:44:21,200 --> 00:44:23,535
‎Your temporary release is canceled
‎as of this moment.

631
00:44:23,619 --> 00:44:25,913
‎Your status as a pretrial inmate
‎has been revoked,

632
00:44:25,996 --> 00:44:27,498
‎and you are officially a fugitive.

633
00:44:27,581 --> 00:44:30,751
‎You are hereby notified ‎that ‎the ‎police
‎have been ordered to arrest you.

634
00:44:30,834 --> 00:44:34,046
‎You are to cancel all other plans
‎and ‎turn ‎yourself ‎in to the nearest--

635
00:44:41,178 --> 00:44:43,806
‎PARK SEUNG-JAE'S FIRST WIN THIS SEASON…

636
00:44:43,889 --> 00:44:46,934
‎GRAND PRIZE: PARK SEUNG-JAE

637
00:45:22,761 --> 00:45:23,679
‎There.

638
00:45:25,180 --> 00:45:27,099
‎-Hello.
‎-Hi.

639
00:45:27,182 --> 00:45:28,851
‎Hi, nice to meet you.

640
00:45:28,934 --> 00:45:30,352
‎-Nice to meet you too.
‎-How are you?

641
00:45:30,436 --> 00:45:31,603
‎Where… Where are we now?

642
00:45:31,687 --> 00:45:33,063
‎We're in…

643
00:45:33,147 --> 00:45:34,565
‎Paradise on earth.

644
00:45:35,357 --> 00:45:36,859
‎Man, it's unbelievably pretty.

645
00:45:36,942 --> 00:45:38,318
‎I should film the ocean.

646
00:45:39,820 --> 00:45:41,155
‎-Careful.
‎-Yeah.

647
00:45:41,238 --> 00:45:42,781
‎I'll hold onto your leg.

648
00:45:43,365 --> 00:45:44,241
‎Min-hwan!

649
00:45:48,704 --> 00:45:49,913
‎What the heck?

650
00:45:55,127 --> 00:45:56,211
‎Seung-jae.

651
00:46:22,070 --> 00:46:23,489
‎There's always a way out.

652
00:46:35,000 --> 00:46:35,834
‎NEW MESSAGE

653
00:46:41,590 --> 00:46:43,342
‎Do you remember the yacht incident
‎from 12 years ago?

654
00:46:44,176 --> 00:46:45,385
‎Let's meet up.

655
00:46:45,928 --> 00:46:47,054
‎From, Park Seung-jae.

656
00:46:59,566 --> 00:47:01,276
‎It's been a while, Cheon Yeo-ri.

657
00:47:02,152 --> 00:47:02,986
‎What are you up to?

658
00:47:03,070 --> 00:47:05,614
‎I'm on a special release,
‎thanks to my father.

659
00:47:07,032 --> 00:47:09,034
‎You're pretty loyal for a friend.

660
00:47:09,117 --> 00:47:11,537
‎Everyone's been avoiding me,
‎but you actually called.

661
00:47:12,621 --> 00:47:14,373
‎What do you have to say
‎about the accident?

662
00:47:16,208 --> 00:47:17,292
‎I knew that'd hook you in.

663
00:47:18,460 --> 00:47:19,670
‎Just talk already.

664
00:47:19,753 --> 00:47:22,172
‎I've yet to place a bigger bet.

665
00:47:23,382 --> 00:47:25,175
‎I'll call you if that doesn't work out.

666
00:47:25,801 --> 00:47:27,052
‎I found someone to blackmail.

667
00:47:28,178 --> 00:47:29,429
‎Someone to blackmail?

668
00:47:30,722 --> 00:47:32,683
‎Blackmail them over what?

669
00:47:32,766 --> 00:47:35,686
‎Do you really not know,
‎or are you pretending not to know?

670
00:47:36,812 --> 00:47:38,188
‎What are you talking about?

671
00:47:38,272 --> 00:47:39,439
‎Just say it straight.

672
00:47:39,523 --> 00:47:41,525
‎I'll call if the deal falls through.

673
00:47:41,608 --> 00:47:42,568
‎Park Seung-jae.

674
00:48:02,379 --> 00:48:03,755
‎Long time no see.

675
00:48:03,839 --> 00:48:04,840
‎How have you been?

676
00:48:11,972 --> 00:48:12,889
‎Hello?

677
00:48:13,849 --> 00:48:14,683
‎Yes.

678
00:48:16,101 --> 00:48:16,935
‎What?

679
00:48:18,186 --> 00:48:20,063
‎Where is that?

680
00:48:25,736 --> 00:48:27,738
‎-He's inside?
‎-Yes.

681
00:48:28,405 --> 00:48:29,489
‎What's he thinking?

682
00:48:29,573 --> 00:48:32,784
‎-Hello, I'm Prosecutor Ma Gang-uk.
‎-Hello.

683
00:48:32,868 --> 00:48:34,786
‎-Where are we headed?
‎-Down that way.

684
00:48:34,870 --> 00:48:35,912
‎-Shall we?
‎-Yes.

685
00:49:18,580 --> 00:49:19,665
‎Who's there?

686
00:49:40,018 --> 00:49:41,103
‎Yeo-ri?

687
00:50:01,581 --> 00:50:03,250
‎How did you know to go there?

688
00:50:03,333 --> 00:50:05,627
‎Park Seung-jae absconded
‎without notifying anyone,

689
00:50:05,711 --> 00:50:07,462
‎and I got a call
‎about his fugitive status.

690
00:50:08,672 --> 00:50:10,716
‎What were you doing there, Yeo-ri?

691
00:50:12,676 --> 00:50:14,511
‎I'll speak with the police.

692
00:50:15,220 --> 00:50:17,806
‎My lawyer will be here soon anyway.

693
00:50:21,977 --> 00:50:24,688
‎Ms. Cheon, I have a few questions for you.

694
00:51:15,238 --> 00:51:16,323
‎Long time no see.

695
00:51:16,406 --> 00:51:17,866
‎How have you been?

696
00:51:17,949 --> 00:51:19,409
‎Why call me to a place like this?

697
00:51:20,577 --> 00:51:21,578
‎A place like this?

698
00:51:23,538 --> 00:51:25,373
‎I just have something
‎to talk to you about.

699
00:51:25,457 --> 00:51:26,792
‎What is it?

700
00:51:26,875 --> 00:51:30,295
‎You can't hide the truth forever,
‎you know.

701
00:51:31,296 --> 00:51:32,839
‎I saw something pretty interesting.

702
00:51:33,340 --> 00:51:34,633
‎I wanted to show it to you too.

703
00:51:37,427 --> 00:51:38,345
‎Ji-hwan.

704
00:51:39,596 --> 00:51:40,430
‎-‎Ji-hwan.
‎-Min-hwan!

705
00:51:41,681 --> 00:51:43,099
‎Min-hwan.

706
00:51:44,476 --> 00:51:45,560
‎Min-hwan!

707
00:51:46,520 --> 00:51:47,354
‎Min-hwan!

708
00:51:48,355 --> 00:51:49,439
‎Kang Min-hwan.

709
00:51:49,981 --> 00:51:52,484
‎Want me to tell you
‎why I avoid the situation?

710
00:51:53,777 --> 00:51:55,403
‎I can argue with you about anything,

711
00:51:56,071 --> 00:51:57,531
‎but nothing will change.

712
00:51:58,114 --> 00:51:59,032
‎What won't change?

713
00:51:59,115 --> 00:52:00,909
‎If I so much as raise my voice at you,

714
00:52:01,952 --> 00:52:03,745
‎do you know how our family looks at me?

715
00:52:05,455 --> 00:52:06,623
‎What do you mean?

716
00:52:09,251 --> 00:52:11,086
‎Tell me. How do they look at you?

717
00:52:19,886 --> 00:52:22,097
‎Forget it. I've had enough.

718
00:52:23,098 --> 00:52:24,683
‎Do you have some kind of victim mentality?

719
00:52:27,602 --> 00:52:28,478
‎What?

720
00:52:30,438 --> 00:52:31,648
‎What's wrong?

721
00:52:42,075 --> 00:52:43,201
‎Ji-hwan.

722
00:52:44,119 --> 00:52:44,953
‎-Ji-hwan.
‎-Min-hwan!

723
00:52:46,705 --> 00:52:47,539
‎Min-hwan.

724
00:52:48,790 --> 00:52:51,084
‎Min-hwan, save me.

725
00:52:51,167 --> 00:52:53,920
‎So Min-hwan was adopted, after all.

726
00:52:54,004 --> 00:52:56,548
‎Could that be why they want to
‎send ‎Min-hwan abroad to study?

727
00:52:58,216 --> 00:52:59,050
‎Min-hwan.

728
00:53:00,218 --> 00:53:02,053
‎Do you have some kind of victim mentality?

729
00:53:03,597 --> 00:53:06,308
‎Min-hwan, what's gotten into you?

730
00:53:07,767 --> 00:53:10,145
‎Min-hwan. No, don't let go.

731
00:53:11,646 --> 00:53:13,815
‎Min-hwan! Don't let go of my hand, okay?

732
00:53:13,899 --> 00:53:14,774
‎Min-hwan!

733
00:53:16,026 --> 00:53:17,819
‎Min-hwan, no! No…

734
00:53:27,871 --> 00:53:31,374
‎I was going through my old stuff
‎and came across this.

735
00:53:34,336 --> 00:53:35,837
‎Here's the deal, buddy.

736
00:53:36,922 --> 00:53:40,508
‎I'm planning to leave the country
‎and never come back.

737
00:53:41,426 --> 00:53:43,428
‎Could you arrange a boat ride?

738
00:53:43,511 --> 00:53:44,804
‎And how about

739
00:53:44,888 --> 00:53:46,306
‎ten billion won on top of that?

740
00:53:47,307 --> 00:53:48,433
‎You've lost your mind.

741
00:53:48,516 --> 00:53:50,310
‎You're the one who lost your mind.

742
00:53:50,393 --> 00:53:52,437
‎I'm not crazy enough
‎to kill my own sibling.

743
00:53:52,520 --> 00:53:54,064
‎All you have is a lousy video.

744
00:53:55,231 --> 00:53:57,233
‎Who would believe a criminal like you?

745
00:53:58,109 --> 00:53:59,527
‎A trial could last a few years,

746
00:53:59,611 --> 00:54:01,488
‎but I'll be acquitted in the end.

747
00:54:01,571 --> 00:54:05,909
‎Wouldn't that ruin your image
‎as a future chairman in the meantime?

748
00:54:06,618 --> 00:54:10,205
‎Hey, you need to think about
‎what you stand to lose.

749
00:54:10,288 --> 00:54:13,333
‎Ten billion won
‎isn't too high a price to pay, is it?

750
00:54:14,292 --> 00:54:16,419
‎I know trash like you all too well.

751
00:54:17,003 --> 00:54:18,838
‎It never ends with ten billion won.

752
00:54:20,006 --> 00:54:21,091
‎It only ends when you die.

753
00:54:22,634 --> 00:54:23,969
‎I'm not getting through to you.

754
00:54:26,763 --> 00:54:29,099
‎I didn't want to go this far, but…

755
00:54:34,729 --> 00:54:36,272
‎Do you think your mother would agree?

756
00:54:37,273 --> 00:54:38,108
‎Hello?

757
00:54:41,277 --> 00:54:42,445
‎What a joke.

758
00:54:45,156 --> 00:54:45,991
‎Call me,

759
00:54:46,658 --> 00:54:47,742
‎all right?

760
00:55:12,308 --> 00:55:13,393
‎Damn it.

761
00:56:00,940 --> 00:56:03,985
‎CHEON YEO-RI

762
00:56:10,700 --> 00:56:12,452
‎NEW MESSAGE: CHEON YEO-RI

763
00:56:16,539 --> 00:56:18,792
‎About the yacht accident 12 years ago.

764
00:56:18,875 --> 00:56:21,336
‎Whatever it is you know,
‎talk to me about it.

765
00:56:22,253 --> 00:56:25,298
‎However much you're blackmailing them for,
‎I'll give it to you.

766
00:56:37,102 --> 00:56:41,856
‎COME MEET ME HERE

767
00:56:41,940 --> 00:56:43,900
‎COME MEET ME HERE

768
00:56:47,403 --> 00:56:48,404
‎Send me the address.

769
00:57:08,967 --> 00:57:09,884
‎Park Seung-jae.

770
00:57:18,685 --> 00:57:19,519
‎Park Seung-jae…

771
00:57:37,370 --> 00:57:39,622
‎Did you hear that Prosecutor Ma
‎was transferred down south?

772
00:57:39,706 --> 00:57:41,124
‎Of course I heard.

773
00:57:41,875 --> 00:57:45,628
‎He's the one who signed the warrants
‎at the last minute for us.

774
00:57:45,712 --> 00:57:47,547
‎People who do their jobs well

775
00:57:47,630 --> 00:57:50,425
‎always ruffle feathers
‎and end up getting sent away.

776
00:57:50,508 --> 00:57:51,509
‎I know, right?

777
00:57:51,593 --> 00:57:54,053
‎There's talk that he's paying
‎for blowing the whistle.

778
00:57:54,137 --> 00:57:57,515
‎Apparently, he reported a chief prosecutor
‎to the Ministry of Justice.

779
00:58:13,239 --> 00:58:16,618
‎Things keep happening
‎like there's a curse.

780
00:58:17,202 --> 00:58:19,287
‎It's better for you
‎that you're getting sent away.

781
00:58:19,370 --> 00:58:21,122
‎It's not.

782
00:58:21,206 --> 00:58:24,042
‎How is Ms. Cheon supposed to
‎fend for herself on her own?

783
00:58:24,125 --> 00:58:26,544
‎Do we have Park Seung-jae's
‎autopsy results?

784
00:58:26,628 --> 00:58:28,087
‎-Not yet.
‎-What about vehicles?

785
00:58:28,171 --> 00:58:31,716
‎We checked footage
‎from all the surveillance cameras nearby,

786
00:58:31,799 --> 00:58:34,552
‎but there was nothing
‎except for a single taxi.

787
00:58:38,348 --> 00:58:39,682
‎I'm going back to the scene.

788
00:58:39,766 --> 00:58:42,227
‎What scene? Park Seung-jae's? What for?

789
00:58:42,310 --> 00:58:44,062
‎Who knows? I might find something.

790
01:00:16,821 --> 01:00:19,866
‎I did as you instructed
‎and canceled your morning appointments.

791
01:00:19,949 --> 01:00:22,118
‎Your schedule's been cleared until 1 p.m.

792
01:00:27,415 --> 01:00:28,333
‎I have this, sir.

793
01:00:29,667 --> 01:00:31,461
‎I think you wore them yesterday,

794
01:00:31,544 --> 01:00:32,962
‎but I only found one.

795
01:01:13,795 --> 01:01:16,255
‎Park Seung-jae was dressed casually,

796
01:01:16,339 --> 01:01:17,965
‎but I found a cuff link at the scene.

797
01:01:18,716 --> 01:01:21,594
‎I'll stop by the local police station
‎on my way back.

798
01:01:21,678 --> 01:01:22,762
‎I'll hand it to them

799
01:01:22,845 --> 01:01:24,889
‎so they can send it
‎to the National Forensic Service.

800
01:01:27,350 --> 01:01:29,769
‎And also… Yes?

801
01:01:29,852 --> 01:01:30,853
‎Hold on.

802
01:01:34,232 --> 01:01:35,233
‎Yeo-ri?

803
01:01:36,359 --> 01:01:37,485
‎Gang-uk!

804
01:02:12,979 --> 01:02:14,188
‎Yeo-ri.

805
01:02:18,860 --> 01:02:19,819
‎Yeo-ri.

806
01:02:20,695 --> 01:02:22,321
‎Wake up, Yeo-ri.

807
01:02:23,281 --> 01:02:24,115
‎Yeo-ri!

808
01:02:28,453 --> 01:02:29,412
‎Yeo-ri!

809
01:03:06,449 --> 01:03:08,826
‎SPOOKY IN LOVE

810
01:03:08,910 --> 01:03:12,455
‎I'm afraid you should
‎prepare ‎yourselves ‎for ‎the ‎worst.

811
01:03:12,538 --> 01:03:14,582
‎-Mr. Ma!
‎-What's wrong?

812
01:03:14,665 --> 01:03:17,210
‎What if Yeo-ri never wakes up?

813
01:03:17,710 --> 01:03:18,920
‎Yeo-ri!

814
01:03:19,837 --> 01:03:21,255
‎Forgive me

815
01:03:21,339 --> 01:03:22,840
‎for taking so long to come.

816
01:03:23,549 --> 01:03:25,259
‎I'm here because I'm desperate.

817
01:03:25,343 --> 01:03:27,595
‎Please help Yeo-ri come back.

818
01:03:27,678 --> 01:03:31,724
‎I'm sure Ji-hwan feels loved
‎even ‎from ‎the ‎other ‎side.

819
01:03:31,808 --> 01:03:32,642
‎Yeo-ri.

820
01:03:32,725 --> 01:03:34,352
‎What about the police?

821
01:03:34,435 --> 01:03:36,938
‎We've handled the surveillance cameras,
‎and they're not up to much.

822
01:03:37,021 --> 01:03:39,106
‎There was a cuff link in my bag.

823
01:03:39,190 --> 01:03:42,318
‎Someone could've caused the accident
‎to get their hands on it.

824
01:03:45,613 --> 01:03:48,741
‎I heard there will be
‎a very important announcement today.

825
01:03:48,825 --> 01:03:49,909
‎Congratulations in advance.

826
01:03:49,992 --> 01:03:52,995
‎I would like to make
‎an important announcement

827
01:03:53,079 --> 01:03:54,705
‎concerning the future of CL Group.

828
01:03:55,665 --> 01:03:56,541
‎Yes.

829
01:03:57,625 --> 01:03:58,751
‎I'm heading inside now.

830
01:03:58,835 --> 01:04:02,296
‎Subtitle translation by: Jennifer Jean Lim
